# ============================================================================
# SUPABASE SETUP (one-time, ~3 minutes)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  1. Go to https://supabase.com -> "New project". Give it a name + a strong
#     database password. Wait ~30 seconds for the project to provision.
#  2. In the project sidebar open: Project Settings -> API.
#  3. Copy "Project URL" into NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL below.
#  4. Copy the "anon public" key into NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY below.
#     (Do NOT use the service_role key here — it bypasses RLS.)
#  5. Open SQL Editor -> New query, paste the contents of
#       supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql
#     and click Run. This creates the profiles + tutor_profiles +
#     student_profiles tables and the signup trigger. Then apply every other
#     file in supabase/migrations/ in numeric order (0002 ... 0009), running
#     each one in turn (through 0021). 0009 seeds the full exam-scoped subject
#     catalog; 0010 renames that catalog's `certificates` table to `exams`;
#     0018 adds the onboarding flag that drives the first-login questionnaire;
#     0019 defaults new tutors to a K–12 year range; 0020 adds the per-day AI
#     generation usage limit; 0021 adds the tutor verification request flow and
#     the notifications table.
#  6. Copy this file to .env.local in the project root and fill in the values.
#  7. Restart `npm run dev` so Next.js picks up the new env vars.
# ============================================================================
#
# AUTH EMAIL (Resend SMTP) — configured in the Supabase dashboard, NOT here.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Supabase sends auth emails (signup confirmation), so there is NO Resend key
#  in this file. The built-in Supabase sender is capped at ~2 emails/hour with
#  poor deliverability; route through Resend instead:
#   1. Create a Resend account -> API Keys -> create a key (re_...).
#   2. Supabase -> Project Settings -> Authentication -> SMTP Settings ->
#        Host smtp.resend.com, Port 465 (or 587), Username resend,
#        Password = your re_... key, Sender name MatchTutor,
#        Sender email onboarding@resend.dev (until a domain is verified).
#   3. Supabase -> Authentication -> Emails -> Confirm signup -> paste
#        supabase/email-templates/confirm-signup.html.
#   4. Supabase -> Authentication -> Rate Limits -> raise emails/hour above 2.
#   5. Supabase -> Authentication -> URL Configuration -> set Site URL.
#  TEST MODE: onboarding@resend.dev only delivers to your own Resend account
#  email. To send to anyone, verify a domain in Resend (SPF/DKIM/DMARC) and
#  switch the Sender email to e.g. noreply@yourdomain.com. See README "Configure
#  auth email (Resend SMTP)".
# ============================================================================
#
# GOOGLE OAUTH — also configured in the Supabase dashboard, NOT here.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  "Continue with Google" uses Supabase's Google provider. The OAuth Client ID
#  and Client secret live in Authentication -> Providers -> Google, so there is
#  NO OAuth key in this file. Also add a wildcard Redirect URL
#  (http://localhost:3000/** for dev) so the app's /auth/callback?next=… matches.
#  See README "Configure Google OAuth".
# ============================================================================
#
# AI PROFILE COPY (Groq) — server-only secret.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  /settings -> About can AI-generate a tutor's tagline + long bio via Groq
#  Cloud (https://console.groq.com -> API Keys). The key is used only on the
#  server (app/api/ai/generate-bio), so it is NOT prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ and is
#  never shipped to the browser. Each tutor is capped at 10 generations/day
#  (enforced by the consume_ai_credit RPC in migration 0020). GROQ_MODEL is
#  optional and defaults to llama-3.3-70b-versatile. Leaving GROQ_API_KEY unset
#  simply disables the feature (the button returns an error).
# ============================================================================

# ============================================================================
#
# TUTOR VERIFICATION + NOTIFICATIONS — server-only secrets.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  A tutor can request verification (/settings + end of /onboarding). The
#  request emails the admin a one-click approve link; approving flips their
#  verified badge and ranks them above unverified tutors. Both "request sent"
#  and "approved" appear on /notifications AND are emailed to the tutor. This
#  needs four server-only values (none NEXT_PUBLIC_):
#   * RESEND_API_KEY — the app sends mail itself here (separate from the auth
#       SMTP above). Resend -> API Keys -> create a key (re_...). Leaving it
#       unset disables sending: emails are logged to the server console instead,
#       so the flow still works locally.
#   * EMAIL_FROM — the From address. Must be on a VERIFIED Resend domain or
#       Resend only delivers to your own account email. Format: "Name <addr>".
#   * ADMIN_EMAIL — where verification requests are sent. Defaults to
#       matchtutoraustralia@gmail.com if unset.
#   * SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — Project Settings -> API -> service_role key.
#       Bypasses RLS; used server-side only to write notifications and approve
#       (the admin has no session when clicking the email link). NEVER expose it.
#   * VERIFICATION_APPROVE_SECRET — any long random string. Signs the approve
#       link's HMAC token (run e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`).
# ============================================================================

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-KEY

GROQ_API_KEY=
GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

RESEND_API_KEY=
EMAIL_FROM=matchtutor <onboarding@resend.dev>
ADMIN_EMAIL=matchtutoraustralia@gmail.com
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
VERIFICATION_APPROVE_SECRET=
